WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.810
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:06.080 --> 00:07.120
(This series is a fictional work created for entertainment purposes.)

3
00:07.200 --> 00:08.240
(The characters, events, locations, organizations agencies, as well as religions, beliefs)

4
00:08.320 --> 00:09.360
(and symbols appearing in this story are presented for storytelling purposes only.)

5
00:09.440 --> 00:10.160
(No intention is made to reference, imply, criticize)

6
00:10.240 --> 00:10.960
(or allude to any individual, organization or religious group)

7
00:12.560 --> 00:14.400
Hey

8
00:20.240 --> 00:24.400
I thought I wouldn't be able to live without you

9
00:24.480 --> 00:28.160
But look at me now

10
00:28.240 --> 00:29.840
I'm shining

11
00:29.920 --> 00:31.640
On nights when the sky turns against me

12
00:31.720 --> 00:34.680
When the rain falls inside my heart

13
00:34.760 --> 00:35.720
I play the same old songs

14
00:35.800 --> 00:37.920
That we used to listen to together

15
00:38.000 --> 00:39.800
Your picture is still right there

16
00:39.880 --> 00:41.560
But I'm not crying anymore

17
00:41.640 --> 00:42.600
I used to want you so badly

18
00:42.680 --> 00:44.000
Now I'm beginning to understand

19
00:44.080 --> 00:46.920
That love comes and go

20
00:47.000 --> 00:48.880
I thought my whole world had to fall apart

21
00:48.960 --> 00:49.680
But in the end

22
00:49.760 --> 00:53.520
It was just my heart learning how to move on

23
00:54.600 --> 00:57.120
I used to say "Can't live without you"

24
00:57.200 --> 00:59.760
But today, I can proudly say, I'm cool

25
00:59.840 --> 01:00.960
I’m looking so good

26
01:01.040 --> 01:03.680
Damn I don’t even try to do

27
01:04.800 --> 01:07.240
Good without you, I’m doing fine

28
01:07.320 --> 01:09.600
Me without you, I can manage

29
01:09.680 --> 01:12.000
Already told you, don’t come back, don’t show your face

30
01:13.200 --> 01:14.280
It's fine.

31
01:49.200 --> 01:50.080
I've found it.

32
02:02.560 --> 02:03.640
Your necklace.

33
02:07.080 --> 02:08.560
Does it belong to your partner?

34
02:13.680 --> 02:15.040
Thank you very much.

35
02:16.440 --> 02:17.800
Please keep your promise.

36
02:34.960 --> 02:36.760
Don't do this to others again. It's not fun.

37
02:37.600 --> 02:38.760
I'm sorry.

38
02:40.040 --> 02:41.800
And thank you for helping me.

39
02:44.640 --> 02:45.480
No problem.

40
02:46.079 --> 02:48.120
From now on, what's between the two of us

41
02:48.200 --> 02:49.920
is only work, nothing but work.

42
02:52.600 --> 02:53.720
Okay.

43
03:32.680 --> 03:34.040
(Ms. Nichakorn, Mr. Teerach, Mr. Seungwoo)

44
03:58.640 --> 03:59.480
(Choi Seungwoo's three rules)

45
03:59.560 --> 04:00.960
(1. No talking about anything except work)

46
04:01.040 --> 04:02.320
(2. Never stay within one meter)

47
04:02.400 --> 04:03.320
(3. Never be alone...)

48
04:05.680 --> 04:08.000
(3. Never be alone together)

49
04:09.720 --> 04:11.240
(3. Never be alone together. Ever.)

50
04:56.240 --> 04:57.320
One meter.

51
05:28.000 --> 05:29.240
Sorry.

52
05:32.320 --> 05:34.440
Dao, perfect timing.

53
05:34.520 --> 05:36.720
I was hoping to trouble you to clean my room.

54
05:37.120 --> 05:39.560
But I already did it, you see.

55
05:39.960 --> 05:40.800
Umm...

56
05:41.360 --> 05:43.400
Did you forget something?

57
05:44.640 --> 05:46.280
I did, though.

58
05:46.360 --> 05:47.280
Not yet.

59
05:47.360 --> 05:48.440
Are you coming?

60
05:49.560 --> 05:50.800
It's almost time for the meeting.

61
05:52.600 --> 05:53.720
No. / No.

62
06:30.840 --> 06:33.000
Where would you like me

63
06:33.080 --> 06:34.400
to clean, Mr. Chat?

64
06:35.960 --> 06:36.960
The mirror, please.

65
06:37.400 --> 06:38.960
Yesterday I tested the color of a new product

66
06:39.040 --> 06:40.680
and it won't come off.

67
06:42.880 --> 06:44.159
Alright.

68
06:50.360 --> 06:52.080
Yesterday you...

69
06:52.159 --> 06:53.720
Hello.

70
06:54.560 --> 06:55.640
I'm almost there.

71
06:56.440 --> 06:58.159
Yes, wait for me for a bit.

72
06:59.600 --> 07:00.440
Oh, right!

73
07:00.520 --> 07:02.640
I've got a whole stack of documents ready for today.

74
07:02.720 --> 07:04.280
I have a presentation to today.

75
07:05.640 --> 07:07.320
I'm certain

76
07:07.400 --> 07:08.960
it'll go well today!

77
07:14.640 --> 07:15.960
Hold on.

78
07:22.040 --> 07:23.560
Excuse me. / Please make a room.

79
07:23.640 --> 07:24.960
Excuse me.

80
07:26.200 --> 07:27.440
Please make way.

81
07:27.920 --> 07:29.560
Thank you.

82
07:41.720 --> 07:43.600
I still can't head home yet.

83
07:43.680 --> 07:44.920
I have to do some more cleaning.

84
07:45.000 --> 07:46.040
It's exhausting.

85
07:46.120 --> 07:48.920
Really. I've been at it since six this morning.

86
07:53.320 --> 07:54.320
It's just too much, isn't it?

87
07:54.400 --> 07:56.040
Hang in there! / We're a day laborer.

88
08:04.000 --> 08:06.240
I'll go clean right away.

89
08:19.800 --> 08:20.880
Are you all right?

90
08:23.080 --> 08:24.000
I'm fine.

91
08:32.880 --> 08:33.880
Thank you.

92
09:02.960 --> 09:04.840
These are the two executives

93
09:04.920 --> 09:07.000
who are partners of our company.

94
09:07.080 --> 09:08.400
They'll be joining our meeting today.

95
09:09.200 --> 09:10.400
Hello everyone.

96
09:10.480 --> 09:12.920
I have fairly high expectations for this new product,

97
09:13.000 --> 09:14.240
and I hope

98
09:14.320 --> 09:16.560
your team won't let us down.

99
09:17.800 --> 09:19.240
The product I want

100
09:19.320 --> 09:22.000
needs a new concept that's on trend

101
09:22.080 --> 09:23.240
and meets the needs of the new generation,

102
09:23.320 --> 09:24.560
and we have limited time.

103
09:24.640 --> 09:25.920
In that case, that's great.

104
09:27.840 --> 09:29.480
Mr. Seungwoo should be well suited to this,

105
09:29.560 --> 09:31.640
since the Korean market has plenty of products of this type.

106
09:32.160 --> 09:34.400
It should be adaptable for our company.

107
09:36.880 --> 09:40.400
However, our user base has diverse skin types,

108
09:40.480 --> 09:42.400
and they also live in different climates.

109
09:42.480 --> 09:44.400
We have someone at the department-head level

110
09:44.480 --> 09:45.720
sent directly from Korea.

111
09:45.800 --> 09:47.240
Something like this should be simple.

112
09:48.920 --> 09:51.400
I'll have the team submit this presentation within two weeks.

113
10:00.920 --> 10:02.320
You can do it right?

114
10:04.360 --> 10:05.200
Of course.

115
10:17.920 --> 10:19.480
This product is really good.

116
10:19.560 --> 10:21.360
Yeah, this one is good.

117
10:21.960 --> 10:23.160
It's pretty good.

118
10:23.240 --> 10:25.400
Hey, I'm going to the canteen first, okay?

119
10:25.480 --> 10:26.440
Sure.

120
10:28.640 --> 10:31.960
Why do I feel like Mr. Teerach and Mr. Seungwoo

121
10:32.040 --> 10:34.520
have a strange vibe between them, somehow?

122
10:34.600 --> 10:36.960
Right? I feel the same way.

123
10:37.360 --> 10:38.960
But if our team

124
10:39.040 --> 10:42.120
gets both Mr. Teerach and Mr. Seungwoo to choose our work,

125
10:45.440 --> 10:47.320
Team B will get fired even sooner.

126
10:47.400 --> 10:49.040
So what should we do?

127
10:54.640 --> 10:56.480
I think I have an idea.

128
11:00.400 --> 11:03.200
I guarantee Team B won't see it coming.

129
11:12.280 --> 11:13.640
Wow.

130
11:16.000 --> 11:16.920
Oh, Mira.

131
11:17.000 --> 11:19.440
I've finished our group's presentation

132
11:19.520 --> 11:20.800
for the color class.

133
11:20.880 --> 11:22.920
All that's left is sending the color-test sample images,

134
11:23.000 --> 11:24.440
and then we can finalize the deck.

135
11:24.840 --> 11:26.040
Okay.

136
11:27.360 --> 11:29.760
Wow, so beautiful.

137
11:31.080 --> 11:32.960
I really can't do this kind of thing.

138
11:33.040 --> 11:34.680
Every time I draw, it turns out a mess.

139
11:35.520 --> 11:36.960
It won't be a mess.

140
11:37.320 --> 11:38.760
You just sketch it first

141
11:38.840 --> 11:43.080
and then color it in the way you drew it, that's all.

142
11:43.160 --> 11:44.400
It's so easy, want to try?

143
11:45.680 --> 11:46.800
Yeah, I'll give it a try.

144
11:47.280 --> 11:48.160
Ah, use this color.

145
11:48.240 --> 11:49.920
Which one? Okay.

146
11:51.960 --> 11:53.640
Pink. / Here, try it.

147
11:54.040 --> 11:55.800
Use this? / Yes.

148
11:55.880 --> 11:56.640
And then dab it on.

149
11:56.720 --> 11:58.280
Dab it on following the lines you've drawn.

150
11:59.160 --> 12:00.560
Draw on the eyes, right?

151
12:00.640 --> 12:01.560
Yes.

152
12:03.880 --> 12:05.760
Hey, it's pretty easy.

153
12:06.880 --> 12:08.720
Right? / Hey, it's actually easy.

154
12:10.320 --> 12:11.560
Put some lipstick.

155
12:12.520 --> 12:13.440
Here.

156
12:13.520 --> 12:14.920
See? It's pretty.

157
12:15.000 --> 12:16.880
Hey! / I told you it was easy.

158
12:16.960 --> 12:18.000
Nice!

159
12:18.520 --> 12:20.280
Actually, if we imagine this

160
12:20.360 --> 12:23.240
as an idea for a cosmetics product, it'd be good, wouldn't it?

161
12:23.320 --> 12:25.360
People using it should find it easy to do their makeup.

162
12:26.240 --> 12:27.440
Come to think of it,

163
12:28.360 --> 12:30.400
that's a good idea.

164
12:37.240 --> 12:39.520
Do you think Seungwoo can handle this project?

165
12:41.360 --> 12:43.080
Well, as Ms. Nichakorn mentioned,

166
12:43.160 --> 12:44.880
there are quite a few differences

167
12:44.960 --> 12:46.200
between the Thai and Korean markets.

168
12:46.280 --> 12:47.240
On top of that,

169
12:47.320 --> 12:49.720
the deadline you have given him is extremely tight,

170
12:50.320 --> 12:51.600
so there's a high risk of failing.

171
12:53.240 --> 12:54.360
If he fails,

172
12:55.000 --> 12:57.000
he'll lose his credibility as well.

173
12:58.720 --> 13:00.280
You're quite clever, Mr. Teerach.

174
13:01.080 --> 13:02.920
It's as if you're giving Seungwoo

175
13:03.000 --> 13:04.280
a chance to prove himself,

176
13:05.000 --> 13:06.440
when in reality, you're just pressuring him

177
13:06.520 --> 13:07.880
into going back to his home country.

178
13:22.600 --> 13:24.160
And shouldn't someone as capable as me

179
13:27.160 --> 13:28.240
get a reward?

180
13:30.080 --> 13:31.440
What kind of reward?

181
13:37.720 --> 13:39.920
We're at work, sir.

182
14:12.600 --> 14:14.120
Rain doesn't start work until late tonight.

183
14:14.640 --> 14:16.680
How about we go find something fun to do in the meantime?

184
14:45.560 --> 14:48.760
Ugh! We only have two weeks!

185
14:48.840 --> 14:50.520
Who could possibly get this done in time?

186
14:50.600 --> 14:51.800
True.

187
14:52.640 --> 14:54.520
And there are so many trending products

188
14:54.960 --> 14:56.400
on the market right now.

189
14:56.760 --> 14:57.760
Which one should we choose,

190
14:57.840 --> 14:59.200
and how can we make it stand out

191
14:59.280 --> 15:01.160
and more appealing than what's already out there?

192
15:03.440 --> 15:04.480
How about lipstick?

193
15:04.920 --> 15:07.240
At the very least, it's something everyone needs,

194
15:07.320 --> 15:08.560
whether they know how to put on makeup or not.

195
15:09.720 --> 15:10.760
That's true.

196
15:10.840 --> 15:13.920
Some people even own several tubes in different colors.

197
15:14.000 --> 15:15.120
Right?

198
15:17.480 --> 15:19.680
I was thinking the same thing as you, Ja.

199
15:19.760 --> 15:21.360
We should go with lipstick since it's currently trending

200
15:21.440 --> 15:22.960
and is also a popular makeup trend.

201
15:23.800 --> 15:25.560
But the real question is,

202
15:25.640 --> 15:27.080
how do we make our product stand out from other brands

203
15:27.160 --> 15:28.800
and appeal to Gen Z?

204
15:29.800 --> 15:30.800
Exactly.

205
15:31.640 --> 15:32.640
Gosh!

206
15:33.320 --> 15:34.840
Have you still not decided on a product yet?

207
15:35.640 --> 15:38.000
Team A has already started working on the designs.

208
15:38.080 --> 15:40.520
Mind your own business. Nobody asked for your opinion.

209
15:40.600 --> 15:44.160
Oh, really? I was just waiting to see the losing team.

210
15:47.600 --> 15:49.440
She's so far away. How could she hear us?

211
15:49.920 --> 15:51.440
So nosy.

212
15:51.520 --> 15:52.560
Why was that wretch here?

213
15:52.640 --> 15:54.040
She was here to bark and stuff.

214
15:54.120 --> 15:55.080
Don't mind her.

215
15:55.160 --> 15:56.200
Always happening.

216
15:56.280 --> 15:57.840
Chat. / Yes?

217
15:57.920 --> 16:01.200
Is this lipstick tester you gave me any good?

218
16:01.280 --> 16:03.360
My niece took it to use, and she says it's great.

219
16:03.440 --> 16:06.240
She says she uses it on her cheeks, eyes, and lips,

220
16:06.320 --> 16:07.920
and she even says if it was a cream,

221
16:08.000 --> 16:10.080
she would cover herself with it.

222
16:10.160 --> 16:11.400
On the whole face, sis?

223
16:11.480 --> 16:14.400
Yes, why? Gen Z is really into it right now.

224
16:18.880 --> 16:20.320
Right? Gen Z loves it.

225
16:20.400 --> 16:21.640
One stick,

226
16:21.720 --> 16:23.200
you can apply it on your eyes, cheeks,

227
16:23.280 --> 16:24.480
and the whole face.

228
16:24.960 --> 16:25.960
Then what do you think

229
16:26.040 --> 16:27.080
if there were a lipstick

230
16:27.160 --> 16:29.000
that works on the eyes, cheeks, and lips,

231
16:29.600 --> 16:30.880
with skincare benefits

232
16:31.360 --> 16:32.720
and long-lasting wear too,

233
16:34.560 --> 16:35.760
would your niece buy it?

234
16:36.200 --> 16:39.120
Oh, if she doesn't buy it, I will!

235
16:39.200 --> 16:40.880
It does everything like that. Right?

236
16:41.800 --> 16:42.800
Right? Would you buy it?

237
16:42.880 --> 16:44.080
Of course.

238
16:45.920 --> 16:47.320
I think I've figured it out.

239
16:50.920 --> 16:52.520
Oh, what are you looking at?

240
16:53.760 --> 16:55.040
I'm scared.

241
16:56.360 --> 16:58.960
Our team is going to create a multifunctional lip gloss.

242
17:01.880 --> 17:04.440
Oh, that's a good idea!

243
17:05.319 --> 17:07.079
Don't forget the tester.

244
17:07.160 --> 17:08.520
Include me too!

245
17:08.599 --> 17:10.440
Don't forget the tester. / Finish it first.

246
17:16.520 --> 17:17.440
Oh, Nueng.

247
17:17.880 --> 17:20.920
Chat, I bought some snacks for you again.

248
17:21.520 --> 17:23.440
Are you trying to fatten me up?

249
17:23.520 --> 17:26.079
Why are you standing here waiting? Is something up?

250
17:26.839 --> 17:28.359
Why do you always know

251
17:28.440 --> 17:30.200
what I would do?

252
17:31.560 --> 17:32.880
If I didn't know, then I'd be crazy.

253
17:35.040 --> 17:36.280
You see,

254
17:36.360 --> 17:38.960
I want to help you with the trend-driven product side,

255
17:39.480 --> 17:43.160
like the design. I think I can help.

256
17:44.120 --> 17:45.440
But I don't think that's appropriate.

257
17:45.840 --> 17:48.240
Still, we're in the same company.

258
17:50.480 --> 17:53.000
But for me, if someone on the team

259
17:53.080 --> 17:54.640
goes to help another team like this

260
17:54.720 --> 17:56.480
while their own work isn't even finished,

261
17:56.960 --> 17:58.200
I'd feel uncomfortable.

262
17:59.520 --> 18:02.040
I just want to help you.

263
18:03.480 --> 18:05.280
These three months, if you slip up...

264
18:05.360 --> 18:06.480
I won't slip up.

265
18:07.320 --> 18:08.280
I'm counting on you.

266
18:08.360 --> 18:09.280
Yes.

267
18:26.120 --> 18:28.400
But thank you anyway.

268
18:49.280 --> 18:50.840
He's pretty popular.

269
19:04.120 --> 19:05.000
(Choi Seungwoo's three rules)

270
19:05.080 --> 19:06.080
(1. No talking about anything except work)

271
19:06.160 --> 19:07.040
(3. Never be alone together. Ever.)

272
19:19.680 --> 19:21.960
"Choi Seungwoo's three rules"

273
19:25.000 --> 19:25.960
What is this?

274
20:10.440 --> 20:12.760
Oh, Chat. You're home.

275
20:13.240 --> 20:15.120
How are you? Are you tired today?

276
20:18.840 --> 20:20.440
Would you like to eat now?

277
20:21.440 --> 20:23.400
It's still warm. It'll be delicious.

278
20:23.480 --> 20:25.800
I'll eat it later. Let me shower first.

279
20:27.560 --> 20:29.640
If it's no longer warm,

280
20:30.680 --> 20:32.800
I can warm it up for you.

281
20:39.200 --> 20:41.040
I'll eat it now, then.

282
20:43.720 --> 20:44.560
Come on.

283
20:51.960 --> 20:52.920
Here you go.

284
20:55.080 --> 20:56.440
Here.

285
20:59.640 --> 21:01.200
Why are you not playing games today?

286
21:03.680 --> 21:04.840
Lately,

287
21:05.440 --> 21:07.240
I've been wanting to change up my routine.

288
21:08.320 --> 21:11.320
I'll only play games when you're not around.

289
21:12.080 --> 21:13.600
But when you are here,

290
21:13.920 --> 21:16.440
I want to spend that time with you.

291
21:27.600 --> 21:29.640
Actually, you don't have to go that far.

292
21:30.360 --> 21:31.440
I know

293
21:33.080 --> 21:34.760
that you don't want to forgive me.

294
21:35.960 --> 21:37.840
But I want to do my best.

295
21:40.600 --> 21:42.880
Can you please give me another chance?

296
21:49.520 --> 21:51.520
Can you please give me another chance?

297
21:55.440 --> 21:57.160
You make it sound like I'm a cruel person.

298
21:57.720 --> 21:58.720
Then...

299
22:00.720 --> 22:02.280
Then please don't stop me.

300
22:06.840 --> 22:07.680
Come on.

301
22:12.680 --> 22:13.520
Here.

302
22:35.680 --> 22:36.720
It tastes good.

303
22:36.800 --> 22:38.200
It's just like Susie's cooking.

304
22:40.600 --> 22:42.080
Because I saw that you

305
22:42.600 --> 22:44.680
enjoy Susie's cooking,

306
22:45.200 --> 22:47.920
I ordered some and had older sibling deliver it.

307
22:53.360 --> 22:54.400
You're trying hard.

308
22:56.240 --> 22:57.080
Yes.

309
22:58.520 --> 22:59.400
Oh!

310
23:00.120 --> 23:01.080
Tomorrow,

311
23:01.960 --> 23:04.440
there's a new movie out that I you like,

312
23:06.360 --> 23:07.600
would you like to go see it together?

313
23:22.240 --> 23:23.360
Hello.

314
23:29.440 --> 23:30.360
Alright.

315
23:35.080 --> 23:36.480
I don't think I can go.

316
23:36.560 --> 23:38.240
I have an urgent matter to attend to tomorrow.

317
24:00.960 --> 24:02.960
One arm's length...

318
24:03.440 --> 24:05.120
How many centimeters is it?

319
24:05.200 --> 24:07.240
A person's arm length

320
24:07.320 --> 24:10.360
is roughly 65 to 70 centimeters.

321
24:12.240 --> 24:13.920
So if one meter...

322
24:40.360 --> 24:41.320
I'm sorry.

323
24:42.680 --> 24:44.240
Thank you for accompanying me.

324
24:45.080 --> 24:47.440
It's your order, so I must come.

325
24:48.960 --> 24:51.920
This is our company's product manufacturing factory.

326
24:52.280 --> 24:53.600
Any product that has been proofed

327
24:53.680 --> 24:55.120
will be sent here to be produced.

328
24:56.800 --> 24:58.440
Everything inside is ready.

329
25:00.080 --> 25:01.000
This way, please.

330
25:10.320 --> 25:11.280
Thank you.

331
25:14.560 --> 25:15.880
Umm... Excuse me. / Yes?

332
25:15.960 --> 25:17.280
How do you wear this?

333
25:17.360 --> 25:19.080
But you've been here quite often.

334
25:21.160 --> 25:22.840
It's Mr. Seungwoo's first time here.

335
25:26.440 --> 25:27.800
I'm counting on you.

336
25:30.160 --> 25:31.560
This way, please.

337
25:35.080 --> 25:36.600
This room is the extract storage room.

338
25:36.680 --> 25:38.480
The extracts we order from our suppliers

339
25:38.560 --> 25:40.400
are delivered and kept here.

340
25:46.080 --> 25:47.800
Let's head to the next room.

341
25:55.480 --> 25:58.080
This is our company's extract mixing machine.

342
25:58.160 --> 26:01.240
We have models from one ton, two tons, three tons, and up.

343
26:03.080 --> 26:04.720
After this, when will it come out?

344
26:05.040 --> 26:07.640
Um, you can ask the staff over there.

345
26:46.200 --> 26:48.760
Have you come up with the project you'll have to pitch yet?

346
26:49.400 --> 26:52.280
My team plans to make a multifunctional lip gloss

347
26:52.360 --> 26:54.840
that can be used on the eyes, cheeks, and lips,

348
26:54.920 --> 26:57.040
emphasizing long-lasting wear and extracts...

349
27:08.880 --> 27:10.120
Interesting idea.

350
27:12.880 --> 27:14.640
So that means it passes, right?

351
27:43.040 --> 27:44.480
It just sounds interesting.

352
27:53.920 --> 27:55.120
You're funny, you know.

353
27:57.120 --> 27:58.120
Do you really think

354
27:58.200 --> 28:00.400
not talking to me about anything except work,

355
28:00.920 --> 28:02.280
standing a meter away from me...

356
28:03.680 --> 28:05.640
and never being alone with me,

357
28:06.440 --> 28:07.800
is actually going to work?

358
28:14.120 --> 28:15.400
You can read this?

359
28:15.480 --> 28:16.720
I couldn't.

360
28:17.400 --> 28:19.160
I just translated it.

361
28:20.760 --> 28:22.080
You're... / It seems like

362
28:23.600 --> 28:25.480
you can't even do any of them.

363
28:30.920 --> 28:31.960
Where are you going?

364
28:33.440 --> 28:34.680
Aren't we leaving together?

365
28:36.480 --> 28:37.960
You should head back on your own.

366
28:53.000 --> 28:55.080
Based on the survey results we got,

367
28:55.160 --> 28:57.720
customers like our product now.

368
28:58.120 --> 28:59.080
Then that's good.

369
28:59.160 --> 29:01.400
It means our first step has passed.

370
29:01.480 --> 29:02.840
But the hard part is

371
29:02.920 --> 29:04.880
how to make our cosmetics have

372
29:04.960 --> 29:06.280
beautiful, long-lasting color

373
29:06.360 --> 29:08.320
within the fairly limited testing time.

374
29:19.840 --> 29:21.160
And I think

375
29:21.600 --> 29:24.880
we should find an expert to help vouch for the extracts,

376
29:25.640 --> 29:28.400
so our team's data looks even more solid.

377
29:28.800 --> 29:30.240
I think that's a good idea,

378
29:30.800 --> 29:33.000
but where are we going to find an expert?

379
29:33.080 --> 29:34.920
We only have one week.

380
29:42.960 --> 29:43.800
You're right.

381
29:45.200 --> 29:48.040
Then, I'll find a way.

382
29:50.960 --> 29:52.080
Chat.

383
29:52.640 --> 29:54.120
And what about this doctor?

384
29:54.200 --> 29:55.920
(You are invited to attend a lecture event)

385
29:57.600 --> 29:59.160
Do you know her?

386
30:01.040 --> 30:02.680
This doctor happens to be giving

387
30:02.760 --> 30:04.600
a special seminar at the university.

388
30:04.680 --> 30:06.240
Shall I try contacting her for you?

389
30:11.560 --> 30:15.000
Come on, let the kid give it a try, there's no harm.

390
30:15.080 --> 30:16.520
We don't have time left.

391
30:23.040 --> 30:23.880
Alright.

392
30:46.800 --> 30:49.440
Seungwoo, how is the project going?

393
30:50.280 --> 30:53.320
At this stage, both teams have interesting ideas.

394
30:54.440 --> 30:56.360
There shouldn't be any problems.

395
31:00.040 --> 31:01.240
There shouldn't be any problems

396
31:01.920 --> 31:03.680
doesn't mean there will be no problems.

397
31:04.720 --> 31:06.200
If you're not confident,

398
31:06.280 --> 31:07.360
you don't have to say anything.

399
31:08.360 --> 31:09.280
Teerach.

400
31:10.800 --> 31:12.120
I mean it, Mom.

401
31:14.360 --> 31:15.640
A team leader

402
31:16.360 --> 31:18.040
should be confident that the work they put out

403
31:18.120 --> 31:19.480
won't have errors,

404
31:20.080 --> 31:21.480
not just assume it will be fine.

405
31:21.920 --> 31:23.360
If a problem comes up,

406
31:24.680 --> 31:26.200
be careful of the responsibilities.

407
31:30.840 --> 31:31.840
I understand

408
31:32.240 --> 31:35.000
that our company may have made mistakes before,

409
31:35.760 --> 31:36.760
but now,

410
31:37.280 --> 31:39.000
I will never let it happen again.

411
31:39.560 --> 31:41.000
Are you trying to insult me indirectly?

412
31:42.240 --> 31:43.280
Calm down.

413
31:43.840 --> 31:44.760
Enough.

414
31:48.720 --> 31:49.880
Will there ever be a day

415
31:50.280 --> 31:52.280
when siblings can just talk nicely to each other?

416
32:08.160 --> 32:09.000
Teerach.

417
32:13.200 --> 32:14.040
Teerach.

418
32:14.400 --> 32:15.640
Please calm down.

419
32:16.200 --> 32:17.040
Show some consideration

420
32:17.120 --> 32:18.640
for your mother in whatever you do.

421
32:18.720 --> 32:20.000
He jabbed at me that much.

422
32:20.080 --> 32:21.520
How am I supposed to stay calm?

423
32:21.600 --> 32:22.920
Nobody jabbed at you, Teerach.

424
32:23.000 --> 32:24.280
You're the one who started it.

425
32:26.800 --> 32:27.960
So you're taking his side?

426
32:29.960 --> 32:31.360
I'm not taking sides.

427
32:32.120 --> 32:33.600
I just don't want you to look bad

428
32:33.680 --> 32:35.240
in your mother's eyes, Teerach.

429
32:36.400 --> 32:38.280
And when I warn you like this,

430
32:38.640 --> 32:39.920
it's because I'm worried about you.

431
32:40.280 --> 32:41.280
Worried?

432
32:42.840 --> 32:45.120
I haven't felt any worry from you at all.

433
32:46.280 --> 32:47.200
Where are you going?

434
32:49.720 --> 32:50.760
That's my business.

435
32:52.000 --> 32:53.760
I'm going to find someone I feel comfortable with.

436
32:57.120 --> 32:58.000
At work,

437
32:59.240 --> 33:00.720
you're with him all the time.

438
33:01.800 --> 33:03.440
Isn't that enough for you, Teerach?

439
33:06.920 --> 33:08.680
At least he doesn't make me feel bad

440
33:08.760 --> 33:10.240
when we're together.

441
33:28.800 --> 33:30.920
Hey, No, guard the base too.

442
33:31.000 --> 33:32.920
Dammit. Farming until ki almost runs out.

443
33:37.480 --> 33:39.160
Hey, heal me a bit. I can't go on any longer.

444
33:47.320 --> 33:49.000
What's wrong with you, Jeno?

445
33:49.600 --> 33:51.360
We've lost three games in a row now, man.

446
33:51.440 --> 33:52.960
Our rank tanked. Dammit.

447
33:53.520 --> 33:54.960
I'm going to the toilet.

448
33:58.920 --> 34:00.400
Yeah.

449
34:11.840 --> 34:15.000
Um... we need your help with something.

450
34:16.639 --> 34:17.560
What is it?

451
34:18.120 --> 34:19.440
Do you happen to have the contact info

452
34:19.520 --> 34:21.280
of the doctor who's coming to give a special lecture

453
34:21.360 --> 34:22.520
at your faculty?

454
34:23.480 --> 34:24.800
Do you mean Professor Thassanee?

455
34:25.800 --> 34:28.480
I've already tried contacting her

456
34:29.199 --> 34:30.600
but couldn't reach her,

457
34:30.679 --> 34:33.120
so I'd like you to be the one to set up an appointment.

458
34:33.199 --> 34:34.400
An appointment about what?

459
34:35.480 --> 34:36.719
You see...

460
34:37.120 --> 34:38.679
I want to make an appointment for...

461
34:39.920 --> 34:40.840
Him.

462
34:43.840 --> 34:45.040
You two are still dating?

463
34:50.639 --> 34:51.800
And if I help,

464
34:53.639 --> 34:54.760
what do I get?

465
35:00.040 --> 35:01.880
Is this color alright?

466
35:02.800 --> 35:04.000
The color is alright.

467
35:05.880 --> 35:07.080
The ingredient.

468
35:12.960 --> 35:13.880
Mr. Chat.

469
35:13.960 --> 35:15.040
Has Team B's product information

470
35:15.120 --> 35:17.480
that's going to Mr. Seungwoo been finalized yet?

471
35:17.560 --> 35:19.400
I need to compile the data

472
35:19.480 --> 35:20.920
to take into the meeting.

473
35:34.080 --> 35:37.080
Then I'll send the preliminary information first.

474
35:37.160 --> 35:39.160
Please let Mr. Seungwoo know that

475
35:39.240 --> 35:42.320
I'll update the data in three days.

476
35:43.360 --> 35:44.280
Okay.

477
35:44.360 --> 35:45.320
Thank you.

478
35:53.120 --> 35:54.160
Dammit.

479
35:54.240 --> 35:55.360
I need to go first.

480
35:56.040 --> 35:57.400
We're running out of time.

481
35:59.080 --> 36:00.280
What to do?

482
36:00.360 --> 36:01.760
How am I going there?

483
36:05.160 --> 36:06.320
Oh, my phone.

484
36:06.400 --> 36:07.240
Okay?

485
36:15.600 --> 36:16.800
When is it arriving?

486
36:17.400 --> 36:19.480
When is the car coming?

487
36:20.400 --> 36:21.720
When is it arriving?

488
36:29.880 --> 36:30.760
Where are you going?

489
36:31.320 --> 36:33.080
Today I have an appointment at 11 a.m.

490
36:33.160 --> 36:35.040
to discuss the extracts for the new product.

491
36:35.440 --> 36:36.960
Sorry for taking leave so suddenly.

492
36:37.880 --> 36:39.880
Get in the car, I'll drive you.

493
36:41.720 --> 36:42.720
It's okay,

494
36:43.160 --> 36:44.440
my ride is almost here.

495
36:45.920 --> 36:47.240
Where is it?

496
36:48.800 --> 36:50.640
Hey, why did it cancel?

497
36:52.360 --> 36:53.720
It's almost 10:30.

498
36:55.600 --> 36:57.120
If you don't make the appointment,

499
36:57.480 --> 36:59.080
Team B won't be able to update the product data

500
36:59.480 --> 37:00.680
in time to compete with Team A.

501
37:06.800 --> 37:07.640
Okay.

502
38:14.000 --> 38:15.280
Excuse me.

503
38:15.360 --> 38:17.720
I have an appointment with Dr. Thassanee at 11 a.m.

504
38:17.800 --> 38:19.400
Where can I go to meet her?

505
38:19.480 --> 38:21.920
Please wait a moment. I'll try to coordinate that for you.

506
38:22.000 --> 38:22.840
Thank you.

507
38:28.920 --> 38:30.680
Who did you say you made the appointment with?

508
38:32.440 --> 38:33.760
Dr. Thassanee.

509
38:33.840 --> 38:36.560
She's a specialist in cosmeceuticals

510
38:36.640 --> 38:38.080
who can issue a certificate for the extracts

511
38:38.160 --> 38:39.840
in our new product.

512
38:45.440 --> 38:47.200
Sorry, but Dr. Thassanee

513
38:47.280 --> 38:49.400
left right after her lecture class this morning,

514
38:49.480 --> 38:51.840
and there's no appointment on her schedule today either.

515
38:52.320 --> 38:53.200
She left?

516
38:53.280 --> 38:54.400
Yes.

517
39:30.960 --> 39:32.040
Chat.

518
39:32.920 --> 39:35.000
I won a game contest today!

519
39:38.560 --> 39:39.400
Here.

520
39:43.080 --> 39:44.200
And...

521
39:45.000 --> 39:47.520
How did your appointment with Dr. Thassanee go?

522
39:48.440 --> 39:49.440
How could you do this?

523
39:53.080 --> 39:54.240
The university staff said

524
39:54.320 --> 39:56.360
no one made an appointment with Dr. Thassanee.

525
39:56.760 --> 39:57.920
What does that mean?

526
40:00.560 --> 40:01.640
You see...

527
40:02.200 --> 40:03.600
I...

528
40:03.680 --> 40:05.200
Did you make an appointment for me?

529
40:08.440 --> 40:09.360
Well...

530
40:09.440 --> 40:11.720
I did try to contact her for you.

531
40:12.640 --> 40:15.360
But I couldn't contact her.

532
40:16.000 --> 40:17.160
So I

533
40:17.520 --> 40:19.200
have a close friend of mine reach out

534
40:19.280 --> 40:20.800
and set up an appointment.

535
40:29.560 --> 40:31.640
I didn't think things would turn out this way.

536
40:32.320 --> 40:34.160
You really ought to know better by now.

537
40:36.160 --> 40:37.280
It's my own fault.

538
40:38.320 --> 40:40.120
I never should have put my hopes on you.

539
40:41.800 --> 40:42.680
Chat.

540
40:44.000 --> 40:44.920
Chat.

541
40:45.000 --> 40:46.200
I'm sorry.

542
40:54.640 --> 40:56.840
Head down a bit. I'm not gonna make it. I'm dead.

543
40:56.920 --> 40:58.440
Hold on. / Yeah, yeah.

544
40:58.520 --> 40:59.760
I need five seconds. I've respawned.

545
41:03.960 --> 41:05.440
Oh, that's tough.

546
41:05.520 --> 41:07.040
I can't go. I'm in the middle. Hold on.

547
41:07.120 --> 41:08.800
Yeah, I'm coming.

548
41:10.000 --> 41:10.920
Hold on.

549
41:14.200 --> 41:15.400
Oh, Jeno. What's the matter?

550
41:20.520 --> 41:21.800
Why did you do that?

551
41:26.240 --> 41:27.080
Did what?

552
41:27.920 --> 41:29.560
If you couldn't set up the appointment,

553
41:30.240 --> 41:31.480
why did you agree to it?

554
41:31.560 --> 41:32.760
Hold on, calm down.

555
41:36.720 --> 41:37.800
Answer me.

556
41:37.880 --> 41:39.240
When did I ever promise?

557
41:40.080 --> 41:41.240
And besides,

558
41:41.320 --> 41:43.720
do you think an ordinary student like me

559
41:43.800 --> 41:44.640
can just set up a meeting

560
41:44.720 --> 41:45.920
with a doctorate-level professor that easily?

561
41:46.000 --> 41:47.440
If you couldn't do it,

562
41:47.520 --> 41:48.720
you should've said so.

563
41:49.480 --> 41:51.200
You made other people suffer for it.

564
41:51.680 --> 41:52.760
Stop blaming other people

565
41:52.840 --> 41:54.560
and blame yourself for once, Jeno.

566
41:55.240 --> 41:56.800
You're so selfish.

567
41:57.160 --> 41:58.640
Do you think I felt nothing

568
41:58.720 --> 42:00.360
about that night?

569
42:01.200 --> 42:02.520
I just slipped up.

570
42:04.360 --> 42:06.240
Then if you felt nothing for me,

571
42:06.320 --> 42:08.080
why did you sleep with me?

572
42:08.840 --> 42:10.520
Then I'll apologize.

573
42:14.920 --> 42:16.200
I'm quitting the team.

574
42:45.280 --> 42:46.440
Excuse me.

575
42:47.720 --> 42:48.880
Mr. Seungwoo.

576
42:49.720 --> 42:50.960
There are only five days left to wrap up

577
42:51.040 --> 42:52.120
the project before the meeting.

578
42:52.200 --> 42:54.600
Team B's data still isn't complete.

579
42:54.680 --> 42:55.960
I will chase it up right away.

580
42:56.880 --> 42:57.800
Understood.

581
43:12.160 --> 43:13.800
Team A has submitted all their data,

582
43:14.120 --> 43:17.160
but Team B still seems to be stuck on something.

583
43:19.080 --> 43:20.680
Only five days left,

584
43:21.120 --> 43:23.360
and Team B's project still isn't coming together.

585
43:25.800 --> 43:28.120
Go check what the problem is.

586
43:28.880 --> 43:29.720
Yes, sir.

587
43:42.400 --> 43:44.320
Hello, I'm Seungwoo.

588
43:52.920 --> 43:54.280
You can park right here.

589
43:56.640 --> 43:57.720
Here you go.

590
44:03.040 --> 44:04.200
You must come with me.

591
44:05.040 --> 44:05.920
Where to?

592
44:07.200 --> 44:09.400
Wait. Where are you taking me to?

593
44:10.000 --> 44:11.640
You must come with me now.

594
44:11.720 --> 44:12.600
This is an order.

595
44:36.360 --> 44:39.080
Oh my gosh! They went together?

596
44:40.440 --> 44:41.840
He even opened the door for him!

597
44:45.080 --> 44:46.520
This is definitely big news.

598
44:52.680 --> 44:55.280
I will make Chat love me like before.

599
44:55.360 --> 44:56.560
It's not that easy, man.

600
44:56.640 --> 44:58.040
Because there are more than

601
44:58.120 --> 44:59.520
one person who has a crush on him.

602
44:59.600 --> 45:00.880
Who dropped you off?

603
45:00.960 --> 45:01.840
My new boss.

604
45:03.280 --> 45:04.600
You like Nueng, right?

605
45:05.240 --> 45:07.400
I think you should just give up on Chat.

606
45:07.480 --> 45:09.040
My name is Leo.

607
45:09.120 --> 45:11.720
I'm a student who will be doing an internship with Team B.

608
45:13.720 --> 45:16.520
Tonight Mr. Seungwoo and Chat have a meeting alone,

609
45:16.600 --> 45:18.960
Go find out for me what they talk about.

610
45:19.040 --> 45:20.000
I play the same old songs

611
45:20.080 --> 45:22.080
That we used to listen to together

612
45:22.160 --> 45:23.840
Your picture is still right there

613
45:23.920 --> 45:25.640
But I'm not crying anymore

614
45:25.720 --> 45:26.640
I used to want you so badly

615
45:26.720 --> 45:28.320
Now I'm beginning to understand

616
45:28.400 --> 45:31.080
That love comes and go

617
45:31.160 --> 45:33.080
I thought my whole world had to fall apart

618
45:33.160 --> 45:34.000
But in the end

619
45:34.080 --> 45:37.480
It was just my heart learning how to move on

620
45:38.760 --> 45:41.160
I used to say "Can't live without you"

621
45:41.240 --> 45:43.800
But today, I can proudly say, I'm cool

622
45:43.880 --> 45:45.000
I'm looking so good

623
45:45.080 --> 45:47.840
Damn I don't even try to do

624
45:48.920 --> 45:51.280
Good without you, I'm doing fine

625
45:51.360 --> 45:53.800
Me without you, I can manage

626
45:53.880 --> 45:56.080
Already told you, don't come back, don't show your face

627
45:56.160 --> 45:58.880
I can still smile, easy and free

628
45:58.960 --> 46:01.280
Good without you, I'm doing fine

629
46:01.360 --> 46:03.760
Me without you, I can manage

630
46:03.840 --> 46:06.000
Already told you, don't come back, don't show your face

631
46:06.080 --> 46:09.160
I can still smile, easy and free

632
46:09.240 --> 46:11.960
You thought I'd cry cry cry all night

633
46:12.040 --> 46:14.440
But I'm dancing under neon lights

634
46:14.520 --> 46:16.960
Without you I'm alright

635
46:17.040 --> 46:20.440
Yeah I'm good without you, good without you

636
46:20.520 --> 46:22.960
Walking in the room now, feeling confident

637
46:23.040 --> 46:26.000
Drip Up Swag Down, Ain't got you to blem

638
46:26.080 --> 46:27.560
Now I'm Feeling loud

639
46:27.640 --> 46:30.120
All Eyes on me Now everybody Shout

640
46:30.200 --> 46:31.520
Don't need anyone to hold my hand

641
46:31.600 --> 46:32.640
Don't need it at all, L O V E R

642
46:32.720 --> 46:33.880
Life got better without having to fake it

643
46:33.960 --> 46:35.560
Thank you for the heartbreak. Ah

644
46:35.640 --> 46:38.240
Used to be someone who cried, but now I level up

645
46:38.320 --> 46:40.440
From a broken heart baby now I double cup

646
46:40.520 --> 46:41.720
